IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `eoa-dates`
IMPORT `eoa-rules`

-- Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) -- the questions of the PERSON WHO SAYS THEY WERE WRONGED.
--
-- SEAT: the individual who says they were discriminated against, sexually harassed or victimised, chiefly at work (a job
-- applicant, an employee, a contract worker, a person invited to be or who is a partner, a person seeking or holding union
-- membership, a person seeking a qualification), and who may bring a dispute to the Commission or apply to VCAT: "Was what
-- was done to me discrimination?", "Is it prohibited, or does an exception let them do it?", "Must my employer accommodate
-- my caring responsibilities, or make adjustments for my disability?", "Was I sexually harassed, and does the Act reach
-- the person who did it?", "Was I victimised for complaining?", "Is my employer liable for what its employee did?", "Can I
-- bring a dispute or a VCAT claim, and can the Commission turn it away as late?". The employer, the Commission and VCAT get
-- no seat: their judgments ("reasonable", "proportionate", "satisfied", "genuine occupational requirement") and what they
-- prove (ss 9(2), 12(6), 13(2), 108(2), 110) are asked as facts.
--
-- Every question takes plain facts (yes/no, dates, a number, a choice from a list) and calls the rules of eoa-rules.l4.
-- The one time limit run as a duty (s 119(3)) is a DEONTIC rule run inside; no question takes a DEONTIC or an EVENT.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Equal
-- Opportunity Act 2010, Version No. 032 (15 April 2026), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria; published with
-- the authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in accordance with
-- the Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Equal opportunity: the questions of the person who says they were wronged`

§§ `What discrimination is`

@export Was the way I was treated on the basis of a protected attribute (Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) ss 6, 7)? The Act protects 21 attributes, and treatment on the basis of an attribute includes one you had in the past, one you are presumed to have, a characteristic people with it generally have or are thought to have, and (for disability) your assistance aid or dog.
GIVEN `which attribute` IS AN `Attribute` @desc The attribute you say you were treated on the basis of: age, breastfeeding, employment activity (asking about or raising concerns about your pay and entitlements), gender identity, disability, industrial activity (union membership or activity), lawful sexual activity, marital status, parental or carer status, physical features, political belief or activity, pregnancy, profession, trade or occupation, race, religious belief or activity, sex, sex characteristics, sexual orientation, an expunged homosexual conviction, a spent conviction, personal association with someone who has one of these, or none of these
      `on what basis` IS A `Basis of the treatment` @desc What the treatment was based on: the attribute you have now, one you had in the past, a characteristic people with it generally have, a characteristic people with it are generally thought to have, an attribute you are presumed to have, your assistance aid, helper or assistance dog, or something else
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Was I treated on the basis of a protected attribute` MEANS
    `s 7(2), (3) -- the treatment was on the basis of an attribute` `which attribute` `on what basis`

@export Was I discriminated against, directly or indirectly (Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) ss 7 to 12)? Direct: you were treated, or were to be treated, unfavourably because of an attribute (a substantial reason, not necessarily the only one; motive and awareness do not matter). Indirect: a requirement, condition or practice disadvantages people with the attribute and the person imposing it cannot prove it is reasonable. A genuine special measure is not discrimination.
GIVEN `which attribute` IS AN `Attribute` @desc The attribute concerned (see the list of 21; or none of these)
      `on what basis` IS A `Basis of the treatment` @desc What the treatment was based on: the attribute now, in the past, a characteristic of it, a presumed attribute, an assistance aid, or something else
      `was I treated unfavourably` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were treated, or someone proposed to treat you, unfavourably (worse than you otherwise would have been: refused, dismissed, given worse terms, humiliated)
      `was the attribute a substantial reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the attribute (or the characteristic or presumption) was a substantial reason for the treatment; it need not be the only or main reason
      `was a requirement imposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a requirement, condition or practice was imposed, or proposed, that applies to everyone (for example a dress code, full-time hours, a fluency test)
      `does it disadvantage people like me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that requirement has, or is likely to have, the effect of disadvantaging people with the attribute
      `was it proved reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who imposed the requirement has shown it is reasonable in all the circumstances (the burden is on them; answer no if they have not)
      `was it a special measure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person has proved the treatment was a genuine special measure to promote equality for a disadvantaged group (answer no if unsure)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Was I discriminated against` MEANS
    `ss 7 to 12 -- I was discriminated against` (`What happened` WITH
        `the attribute concerned`                 IS `which attribute`
        `the basis of what was done`              IS `on what basis`
        `I was treated unfavourably`              IS `was I treated unfavourably`
        `the attribute was a substantial reason`  IS `was the attribute a substantial reason`
        `a requirement was imposed`               IS `was a requirement imposed`
        `the requirement disadvantages people with the attribute` IS `does it disadvantage people like me`
        `the requirement was proved reasonable`   IS `was it proved reasonable`
        `it was proved to be a special measure`   IS `was it a special measure`)

@export Is the program or measure that excluded me a special measure, so that it is not discrimination (Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) s 12)? It must be in good faith, reasonably likely to achieve substantive equality for the group, proportionate, and justified by the group's particular need; it stops being one once its purpose is achieved. The person running it must prove it.
GIVEN `is it in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the measure is undertaken in good faith to promote substantive equality for a group with a particular attribute
      `is it likely to work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is reasonably likely to achieve that purpose
      `is it proportionate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a proportionate means of achieving it
      `does the group have a particular need` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is justified because members of the group have a particular need for advancement or assistance
      `has its purpose been achieved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the purpose has now been achieved
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is it a special measure` MEANS
    `s 12 -- the measure is a special measure` `is it in good faith` `is it likely to work` `is it proportionate` `does the group have a particular need` `has its purpose been achieved`

§§ `Discrimination at work (Part 4 Divisions 1 and 2)`

@export Is what my employer (or principal, firm, union or qualifying body) did to me discrimination the Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) prohibits (ss 13, 16, 18, 21, 30, 31, 35, 36)? It is prohibited if it is in one of the areas the Act lists for your position, it is discrimination, and no exception or exemption is proved. Firms of fewer than 5 partners may discriminate reasonably.
GIVEN `my position` IS A `Work position` @desc Your position: a job applicant, a person offered employment, an employee, a contract worker (working for a principal under your employer's contract), a person invited to join a firm being established, a person invited or seeking to become a partner, a partner, a person seeking to join a union or other industrial organisation, a member of one, or a person seeking or holding an occupational qualification (licence, registration)
      `what was done` IS A `What was done to me` @desc What was done: deciding who to offer the job, partnership or membership; the terms offered; refusing or failing to give you the job, membership or qualification; denying a guidance, apprenticeship or training program; denying or limiting promotion, transfer, training or benefits; dismissing or expelling you or taking away membership or a qualification; not allowing you to work; the terms on which you may work; varying membership or qualification terms; some other detriment
      `does the firm have 5 or more partners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a firm (or one being established): whether it has, or will have, 5 or more partners (answer yes if not a firm)
      `was I discriminated against` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were discriminated against, directly or indirectly, on the basis of a protected attribute (see the question "Was I discriminated against")
      `was the small firm's discrimination reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the firm has fewer than 5 partners: whether its discrimination was reasonable (answer no otherwise)
      `would it be lawful if my employer did it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are a contract worker: whether the same thing would not contravene the Act if your own employer did it (answer no otherwise)
      `has an exception been proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer or other body has proved that an exception or exemption applies (see the exception questions; the burden is on them; answer no if unsure)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is it prohibited discrimination at work` MEANS
    `Part 4 Divisions 1 and 2 -- the discrimination is prohibited` `my position` `what was done` `does the firm have 5 or more partners` (JUST `was I discriminated against`) `was the small firm's discrimination reasonable` `would it be lawful if my employer did it` `has an exception been proved`

@export Did my employer (or principal, or firm) unlawfully refuse to accommodate my responsibilities as a parent or carer in my work arrangements (Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) ss 17, 19, 22, 32)? The duty is owed to a person offered employment, an employee, a contract worker, and a partner or person invited to be one in a firm of 5 or more partners; only an unreasonable refusal is prohibited.
GIVEN `my position` IS A `Work position` @desc Your position (job applicant, person offered employment, employee, contract worker, partner or person invited to be one, union member or applicant, person dealing with a qualifying body)
      `does the firm have 5 or more partners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a firm: whether it has 5 or more partners (answer yes if not a firm)
      `am I a parent or carer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have responsibilities as a parent (including step-, adoptive, foster parent or guardian) or as a carer (someone wholly or substantially dependent on you for ongoing care, not on a commercial basis)
      `was the refusal unreasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the refusal to accommodate those responsibilities (for example a request for different hours or to work from home) was unreasonable, weighing your circumstances, the role, the arrangements needed, the employer's size, finances and business, and the consequences for each side
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Was the refusal to accommodate my caring responsibilities unlawful` MEANS
    `ss 17, 19, 22, 32 -- the refusal to accommodate me is prohibited` `my position` `does the firm have 5 or more partners` `am I a parent or carer` `was the refusal unreasonable`

@export Must my employer (or principal, or firm) make this adjustment for my disability (Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) ss 20, 22A, 33)? It must make reasonable adjustments you need to perform the genuine and reasonable requirements of the work, unless you could not do them even after the adjustments, or it has complied with a disability standard or a building determination on the point.
GIVEN `my position` IS A `Work position` @desc Your position (job applicant, person offered employment, employee, contract worker, partner or person invited to be one, union member or applicant, person dealing with a qualifying body)
      `do I have a disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a disability (loss or malfunction of a bodily or mental function or part, disease organisms, disfigurement, a learning condition; including a future disability)
      `do I need adjustments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you need adjustments (a ramp, software, changed instructions, time off for treatment, more breaks) to perform the genuine and reasonable requirements of the work
      `could I do the work after them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, with the adjustments made, you could adequately perform those requirements (considering your training, qualifications, experience and current performance)
      `is the adjustment reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the adjustment is reasonable, weighing your circumstances, the role, the adjustment, the employer's size, finances and business, the effect on the workplace and the consequences for each side
      `has a disability standard been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer has complied with, or been exempted from, a Commonwealth disability standard on the subject of this adjustment (answer no if unsure)
      `has a building determination been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the adjustment concerns a building or land covered by a determination under s 160B of the Building Act 1993 that the employer complies with (answer no if unsure)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must they make this adjustment for my disability` MEANS
    `ss 20, 22A, 33 -- they must make the adjustment` `my position` `do I have a disability` `do I need adjustments` `could I do the work after them` `is the adjustment reasonable` `has a disability standard been complied with` `has a building determination been complied with`

§§ `Exceptions an employer may prove (ss 23 to 29, 34, 37, 75, 76, 82A, 83A, 86)`

@export Can my employer (or firm) rely on the disability exception, because the adjustments I need are not reasonable or I could not do the work even with them (Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) ss 23, 34)? The employer must first have met the duty paragraph (b) names (for an employer, the adjustment duty in s 20; for a firm, as printed, s 32).
GIVEN `my position` IS A `Work position` @desc Your position (job applicant, person offered employment, employee, a firm position, or another)
      `which attribute` IS AN `Attribute` @desc The attribute the discrimination was on the basis of
      `do I need adjustments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you need adjustments to perform the genuine and reasonable requirements of the work or partnership
      `did they comply with the named duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an employer: whether it made the reasonable adjustments s 20 requires; for a firm: whether it met s 32 (not unreasonably refusing to accommodate parent or carer responsibilities)
      `does the firm have 5 or more partners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a firm: whether it has 5 or more partners (answer yes if not a firm)
      `am I a parent or carer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have responsibilities as a parent or carer
      `are the adjustments unreasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the adjustments you need are not reasonable adjustments
      `could I not do the work even with them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you could not adequately perform the genuine and reasonable requirements even after the adjustments
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can they rely on the disability exception` MEANS
    `ss 23, 34 -- the disability exception applies` `my position` `which attribute` `do I need adjustments` `did they comply with the named duty` `does the firm have 5 or more partners` `am I a parent or carer` `are the adjustments unreasonable` `could I not do the work even with them`

@export Can the employer choose who to hire for domestic or personal services (including child care) on otherwise prohibited grounds (Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) s 24)? Only in deciding who to offer the job, for work in the employer's own home, or in a client's home at the client's request where the employer is in that business.
GIVEN `my position` IS A `Work position` @desc Your position (a job applicant or person offered employment, or another)
      `what was done` IS A `What was done to me` @desc What was done (the exception covers only deciding who should be offered the job)
      `is it domestic or personal services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the job is providing domestic or personal services, including caring for, instructing or supervising children
      `where is the work` IS A `Where the domestic services are given` @desc Where the services are given: in the employer's own home, in a client's home at the client's request, in a client's home without such a request, or elsewhere
      `is the employer in that business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is in the business of providing domestic or personal services to others
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can they rely on the domestic services exception` MEANS
    `s 24 -- the domestic services exception applies` `my position` `what was done` `is it domestic or personal services` `where is the work` `is the employer in that business`

@export Can the employer rely on the care of children exception (Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) s 25)? It covers hiring and employment involving the care, instruction or supervision of children, where the discrimination is reasonably necessary to protect their wellbeing, but not employment by a post-secondary education provider.
GIVEN `my position` IS A `Work position` @desc Your position (job applicant, person offered employment, employee, or another)
      `does the job involve children` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the job involves the care, instruction or supervision of children (under 18)
      `is it reasonably necessary to protect them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the discrimination is reasonably necessary to protect the children's physical, psychological or emotional wellbeing
      `is the employer post-secondary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is a post-secondary education provider (a university, TAFE or other provider under the Education and Training Reform Act 2006)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can they rely on the care of children exception` MEANS
    `s 25 -- the care of children exception applies` `my position` `does the job involve children` `is it reasonably necessary to protect them` `is the employer post-secondary`

@export Can the employer limit the job offer on the basis of a genuine occupational requirement (Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) s 26)? Sex where it is a genuine requirement (physical characteristics, fitting clothing, searches, lavatories, undress areas); age, sex, race or disability for authenticity or credibility; physical features in performance, photographic or modelling work; experience in a profession, trade or occupation where it is a genuine and reasonable requirement.
GIVEN `my position` IS A `Work position` @desc Your position (a job applicant or person offered employment, or another)
      `what was done` IS A `What was done to me` @desc What was done (the exception covers the offering of employment: deciding who, the terms, refusing)
      `which attribute` IS AN `Attribute` @desc The attribute the offer was limited by
      `why one sex` IS A `Why one sex is required` @desc If limited to one sex, why: physical characteristics only that sex has (not strength or stamina), fitting clothing, searching people of that sex, entering a lavatory in use by that sex, entering areas where that sex is undressed, another genuine occupational requirement, or none
      `is it needed for authenticity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether limiting the offer (by age, sex, race or disability) is necessary for authenticity or credibility, as in a dramatic or artistic performance, entertainment, photographic or modelling work
      `is it performance or modelling work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the job is a dramatic or artistic performance, photographic or modelling work, or similar
      `is the experience a genuine requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the offer turned on your profession, trade or occupation: whether experience in a particular one is relevant, a genuine occupational requirement for the role, and reasonable to insist on
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can they rely on a genuine occupational requirement` MEANS
    `s 26 -- a genuine occupational requirement exception applies` `my position` `what was done` `which attribute` `why one sex` `is it needed for authenticity` `is it performance or modelling work` `is the experience a genuine requirement`

@export Can the employer refuse me a job on the basis of my political belief or activity, because the job is political staff work (Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) s 27)?
GIVEN `my position` IS A `Work position` @desc Your position (a job applicant or person offered employment, or another)
      `which attribute` IS AN `Attribute` @desc The attribute the offer turned on
      `is it political staff work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the job is as a ministerial adviser, member of staff of a political party, electorate staff of any person, or similar
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can they rely on the political employment exception` MEANS
    `s 27 -- the political employment exception applies` `my position` `which attribute` `is it political staff work`

@export Can the employer limit the job to people with a particular attribute because it provides welfare services to people with that attribute (Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) s 28)? The services must be a special measure or a special needs service, best provided by people with the attribute.
GIVEN `my position` IS A `Work position` @desc Your position (a job applicant or person offered employment, or another)
      `are the services for that group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the job is in providing services for people with the particular attribute
      `are they a special measure or special needs service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether those services are a special measure (s 12) or a special needs service (s 88)
      `are they best provided by people with the attribute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they can be provided most effectively by people with that attribute
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can they rely on the welfare services exception` MEANS
    `s 28 -- the welfare services exception applies` `my position` `are the services for that group` `are they a special measure or special needs service` `are they best provided by people with the attribute`

@export May my employer pay me according to my age, as a youth wage (Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) s 28A)? Only employees under 21.
GIVEN `my position` IS A `Work position` @desc Your position (an employee, or another)
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May I be paid a youth wage` MEANS
    `s 28A -- I may be paid a youth wage` `my position` `my age`

@export May my employer take my age (and my eligibility for a superannuation retirement benefit) into account in the terms of an offer to resign or retire early (Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) s 29)?
GIVEN `my position` IS A `Work position` @desc Your position (an employee, or another)
      `is it a retirement incentive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is deciding the terms of an incentive offered to you to resign or retire
      `which attribute` IS AN `Attribute` @desc The attribute taken into account (age, or another)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can they rely on the early retirement exception` MEANS
    `s 29 -- the early retirement exception applies` `my position` `is it a retirement incentive` `which attribute`

@export May the qualifying body set or vary the terms of my occupational qualification to let me practise with my disability (Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) s 37)?
GIVEN `my position` IS A `Work position` @desc Your position (a person dealing with a qualifying body, or another)
      `which attribute` IS AN `Attribute` @desc The attribute concerned (disability, or another)
      `are the terms reasonable and enabling` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the terms or variations are reasonable and set to enable you, with your disability, to practise the profession, trade or occupation
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the qualifying body rely on the reasonable terms exception` MEANS
    `s 37 -- the qualification terms exception applies` `my position` `which attribute` `are the terms reasonable and enabling`

@export Can the person rely on the exception for things another law or a court order requires (Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) ss 75, 76)? It applies where the discrimination is necessary to comply with, or authorised by, another Act or enactment, or necessary to comply with an order of VCAT, another tribunal or a court.
GIVEN `did another law require or authorise it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the discrimination was necessary to comply with, or authorised by, a provision of another Act or enactment (not this Act)
      `did a court or tribunal order require it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was necessary to comply with an order of VCAT, another tribunal or a court
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can they rely on the statutory authority exception` MEANS
    `ss 75, 76 -- the statutory authority or court order exception applies` `did another law require or authorise it` `did a court or tribunal order require it`

@export Can a religious body or religious school employer rely on the religious employment exception (Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) ss 82A, 83A)? Only for religious belief or activity, where conformity with the religion is an inherent requirement of the position, you cannot meet it because of your religious belief or activity, and the discrimination is reasonable and proportionate.
GIVEN `is the employer religious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer is a religious body, or a body running a school or other educational institution conducted in accordance with religious doctrines, beliefs or principles
      `which attribute` IS AN `Attribute` @desc The attribute the discrimination was on the basis of
      `is conformity an inherent requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether conformity with the religion's doctrines, beliefs or principles is an inherent requirement of the particular position
      `can I not meet it because of my religion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you cannot meet that requirement because of your religious belief or activity
      `is it reasonable and proportionate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the discrimination is reasonable and proportionate in the circumstances
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can they rely on the religious employment exception` MEANS
    `ss 82A, 83A -- the religious employer exception applies` `is the employer religious` `which attribute` `is conformity an inherent requirement` `can I not meet it because of my religion` `is it reasonable and proportionate`

@export Can the person rely on the health, safety and property exception (Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) s 86)? For disability or physical features where reasonably necessary to protect anyone's health or safety, or property; for pregnancy where reasonably necessary to protect health or safety.
GIVEN `which attribute` IS AN `Attribute` @desc The attribute the discrimination was on the basis of
      `is it needed for health or safety` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the discrimination is reasonably necessary to protect the health or safety of any person (including you) or the public
      `is it needed to protect property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is reasonably necessary to protect the property of any person or public property
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can they rely on the health and safety exception` MEANS
    `s 86 -- the health, safety and property exception applies` `which attribute` `is it needed for health or safety` `is it needed to protect property`

§§ `The positive duty (Part 3) -- whether it binds them, and what can be done about a breach`

@export Does the positive duty to eliminate discrimination, sexual harassment and victimisation bind the person or organisation I am dealing with (Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) s 15)? It binds anyone with a duty under Part 4, 6 or 7 (every employer, principal, firm, union, qualifying body), to take reasonable and proportionate measures. You cannot bring a dispute or VCAT claim about a breach of it; the Commission may investigate.
GIVEN `do they have a duty not to discriminate, harass or victimise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they have a duty under Part 4, 6 or 7 not to discriminate, sexually harass or victimise (an employer, principal, firm, union, qualifying body, service provider, landlord, school, club or council does)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does the positive duty bind them` MEANS
    `s 15 -- the positive duty binds them` `do they have a duty not to discriminate, harass or victimise`

@export Can the Commission investigate the matter I have reported, such as a breach of the positive duty (Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) ss 15(4), 127)? It may if the issue is serious, affects a class or group, cannot reasonably be resolved by dispute resolution or a VCAT claim, there are reasonable grounds to suspect a contravention, and an investigation would advance the Act's objectives.
GIVEN `is it serious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the matter raises an issue that is serious in nature
      `does it affect a group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it relates to a class or group of persons, not just you
      `can it not be resolved otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it cannot reasonably be expected to be resolved by dispute resolution or a VCAT application
      `are there reasonable grounds to suspect a contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there are reasonable grounds to suspect one or more contraventions of the Act
      `would it advance the objectives` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an investigation would advance the Act's objectives
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the Commission investigate` MEANS
    `s 127 -- the Commission may investigate` `is it serious` `does it affect a group` `can it not be resolved otherwise` `are there reasonable grounds to suspect a contravention` `would it advance the objectives`

§§ `Sexual harassment (Part 6)`

@export Was I sexually harassed, in a relationship or place the Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) covers (ss 92 to 102)? Sexual harassment is an unwelcome sexual advance, request for sexual favours or other conduct of a sexual nature, where a reasonable person would have anticipated you would be offended, humiliated or intimidated. At work it covers employers, co-workers, anyone at a shared workplace, partners, unions and qualifying bodies, and volunteers and unpaid workers too. No exception lets it happen.
GIVEN `what kind of conduct` IS A `Kind of conduct` @desc What was done: an unwelcome sexual advance, an unwelcome request for sexual favours, other unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature (touching, remarks with sexual connotations, sexual gestures or comments in your presence), or conduct that was welcome or not sexual
      `would a reasonable person have anticipated offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a reasonable person, having regard to all the circumstances, would have anticipated that you would be offended, humiliated or intimidated
      `who did it` IS A `Who harassed me` @desc Who did it: your employer or prospective employer; someone employed by your employer; someone you employ; someone at a place that is a workplace of you both; a partner in your firm; a member or employee of your union; a member or employee of a qualifying body; staff, a student or authority member at your educational institution; someone providing or receiving goods or services; someone providing accommodation to you; a club member; a fellow councillor; or someone in none of these relationships
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Was I sexually harassed in breach of the Act` MEANS
    `Part 6 -- the sexual harassment is prohibited` `what kind of conduct` `would a reasonable person have anticipated offence` `who did it`

§§ `Victimisation and the liability of others (Part 7)`

@export Was I victimised (Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) ss 103, 104)? It is victimisation to subject you, or threaten to subject you, to any detriment because you or someone associated with you complained, brought a dispute or proceedings, gave evidence or information, attended a VCAT conference, alleged a contravention (unless false and in bad faith) or refused to contravene the Act, or because they believe you did or will.
GIVEN `what was done` IS A `What I or my associate did` @desc What you (or someone associated with you) did, or were believed to have done or to intend: brought a dispute to the Commission; complained under the old Act or the Racial and Religious Tolerance Act; brought other proceedings; gave evidence, information or a document; attended a VCAT compulsory conference or mediation; did anything else in accordance with the Act; alleged someone contravened the Act; refused to do something that would contravene it; or none of these
      `was I subjected or threatened with a detriment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were subjected, or threatened with, any detriment (dismissal, demotion, exclusion, worse treatment, humiliation)
      `was that a substantial reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what you did (or were believed to have done) was a substantial reason for it, not necessarily the only or main one
      `was the allegation false and in bad faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you alleged a contravention: whether the allegation was false and not made in good faith (answer no otherwise)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Was I victimised` MEANS
    `s 104 -- I was victimised` `what was done` `was I subjected or threatened with a detriment` `was that a substantial reason` `was the allegation false and in bad faith`

@export Can I bring my dispute or VCAT claim against the person who instructed, encouraged or helped the person who discriminated against, harassed or victimised me (Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) ss 105, 106)?
GIVEN `did they instruct or help` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person requested, instructed, induced, encouraged, authorised or assisted another person to contravene the Act
      `did the other person contravene as a result` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, as a result, the other person did contravene it against you
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I claim against the person who instructed or helped` MEANS
    `ss 105, 106 -- I can bring my claim against the person who authorised or assisted` `did they instruct or help` `did the other person contravene as a result`

@export Was it unlawful for the employer (or anyone) to ask me for this information (Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) ss 107, 108)? It may not ask for information that could be used to discriminate against you, unless it proves the information is reasonably required for a purpose that does not involve prohibited discrimination.
GIVEN `could the information be used to discriminate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the information asked for (age, marital status, health, plans for children, religion) could be used to form the basis of discrimination against you
      `did they prove a legitimate need` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they have proved the information is reasonably required for a purpose that does not involve prohibited discrimination (answer no if they have not)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Was the request for my information unlawful` MEANS
    `ss 107, 108 -- the request for information is prohibited` `could the information be used to discriminate` `did they prove a legitimate need`

@export Must the person who lawfully collected my information destroy or permanently de-identify it now (Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) s 108(3)(b))?
GIVEN `is it still needed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the information is still required for the non-discriminatory purpose it was collected for
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must they destroy my information` MEANS
    `s 108(3)(b) -- they must destroy or de-identify my information` `is it still needed`

@export Is the person who lawfully collected my information forbidden to pass it on (Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) s 108(3)(a))? They may disclose it only where necessary for the non-discriminatory purpose.
GIVEN `is disclosure necessary for the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether disclosing or communicating the information is necessary for the non-discriminatory purpose it was collected for
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Are they forbidden to pass my information on` MEANS
    `s 108(3)(a) -- they must not pass my information on` `is disclosure necessary for the purpose`

@export Is the employer (or principal) also liable for the discrimination, harassment or victimisation its employee or agent did to me (Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) ss 109, 110)? Both are taken to have contravened, and you may claim against either or both, unless the employer proves it took reasonable precautions.
GIVEN `were they acting in their employment or as agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who did it was acting in the course of their employment or as the employer's (or principal's) agent
      `does it contravene the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what they did contravenes Part 4, 6, 6A or 7, or would if the employer or principal had done it
      `did the employer prove reasonable precautions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer or principal has proved, on the balance of probabilities, that it took reasonable precautions to prevent it (policies, training, complaint handling; answer no if not proved)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is the employer liable too` MEANS
    `ss 109, 110 -- the employer or principal is liable too` `were they acting in their employment or as agent` `does it contravene the Act` `did the employer prove reasonable precautions`

§§ `Bringing a dispute or a VCAT claim (Part 8)`

@export Can I (or someone for me) bring a dispute to the Victorian Equal Opportunity and Human Rights Commission, or apply directly to VCAT, about this (Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) ss 15(3), 113, 122, 123)? Both routes cover contraventions of Parts 4, 6, 6A and 7; you can go to VCAT whether or not you went to the Commission, and the Act sets no time limit for VCAT. A breach of the positive duty alone cannot be brought.
GIVEN `what is it about` IS A `What my claim is about` @desc What you say was contravened: discrimination (Part 4), sexual harassment (Part 6), vilification (Part 6A), victimisation or another Part 7 contravention, only a breach of the positive duty in s 15, or only an offence such as discriminatory advertising
      `who is bringing it` IS A `Who is bringing it` @desc Who brings it: you, about a contravention in relation to you; a person you authorised because your disability prevents you; anyone for you if your disability prevents you authorising; your parent if you are a child; another person for you as a child with consent the Commission or VCAT accepts; another person for you as a child without that consent; or another person in none of these ways
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I bring a dispute or VCAT claim` MEANS
    `ss 113, 122, 123 -- the dispute or application can be brought` `what is it about` `who is bringing it`

@export Can the Commission decline to deal with my dispute, for example because it is more than 12 months late (Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) s 116)? The Commission may decline if the contravention was more than 12 months before you brought the dispute, the matter has been adequately dealt with or belongs in a court or tribunal, proceedings have started elsewhere, or it considers dispute resolution not appropriate. A decline does not stop a VCAT application.
GIVEN `day of the contravention` IS A DATE @desc The day the conduct you complain of happened (for continuing conduct, the last day)
      `day I brought the dispute` IS A DATE @desc The day you brought (or will bring) the dispute to the Commission
      `was it adequately dealt with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the matter has already been adequately dealt with by a court or tribunal
      `does it belong in a court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it involves subject matter more appropriately dealt with by a court or tribunal
      `are proceedings on elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether anyone has started proceedings about it in another forum (for example the Fair Work Commission or the Australian Human Rights Commission)
      `does the Commission think it inappropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commission considers, in all the circumstances, that dispute resolution is not appropriate (answer no if unsure)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the Commission decline my dispute` MEANS
    `s 116 -- the Commission may decline my dispute` `day of the contravention` `day I brought the dispute` `was it adequately dealt with` `does it belong in a court` `are proceedings on elsewhere` `does the Commission think it inappropriate`

@export Was the conduct I complain of more than 12 months before I brought my dispute, so that the Commission may decline it on that ground (Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) s 116(a))? Exactly 12 months is not more than 12 months.
GIVEN `day of the contravention` IS A DATE @desc The day the conduct you complain of happened
      `day I brought the dispute` IS A DATE @desc The day you brought (or will bring) the dispute to the Commission
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my dispute more than 12 months late` MEANS
    `s 116(a) -- the contravention was more than 12 months before the dispute` `day of the contravention` `day I brought the dispute`

@export Has dispute resolution at the Commission ended (Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) s 115)? It starts when you tell the Commission you wish to proceed, and ends when the Commission declines, a party withdraws, or the parties reach agreement. Withdrawing does not stop you applying to VCAT (s 118).
GIVEN `did I tell the Commission to proceed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have told the Commission you wish to proceed with dispute resolution
      `did the Commission decline` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commission has declined to provide or continue it
      `did a party withdraw` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or the other party has told the Commission you no longer wish to take part
      `was agreement reached` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the parties have reached agreement about the subject matter
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Has dispute resolution ended` MEANS
    `s 115 -- dispute resolution has ended` `did I tell the Commission to proceed` `did the Commission decline` `did a party withdraw` `was agreement reached`

@export Can what was said or done in the Commission's dispute resolution be used as evidence at VCAT or in court (Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) s 117)? Not in a proceeding about the subject matter of the dispute.
GIVEN `was it said or done in dispute resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the statement, offer or act was made in the course of the Commission's dispute resolution
      `is the proceeding about the same matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the VCAT or court proceeding relates to the subject matter of that dispute
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can it be used as evidence` MEANS
    `s 117 -- it can be used as evidence` `was it said or done in dispute resolution` `is the proceeding about the same matter`

@export Is (or was) my request for a written record of our settlement agreement in time (Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) s 119(3))? It must be made within 30 days after the agreement is reached; a late request does not affect the agreement's validity.
GIVEN `day the agreement was reached` IS A DATE @desc The day the parties reached agreement
      `have I asked for a record` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (or another party) have asked for a written record of the agreement
      `day I asked` IS A DATE @desc The day the request was made (any date if not yet)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `What became of the request`
`Is my request for a settlement record in time` MEANS
    `s 119(3) -- what became of my request for a record` `day the agreement was reached` `have I asked for a record` `day I asked` `today`

@export Must VCAT register my settlement agreement, so that it can be enforced as a VCAT order (Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) s 120)? After written notice to the other party you may lodge the signed and certified record; VCAT must register it unless it considers it may not be practicable to enforce or supervise.
GIVEN `is the record signed by each party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the written record of agreement is signed by or on behalf of each party
      `has the Commission certified it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commission has certified the record
      `did I notify the other party in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you notified the other party in writing before lodging it
      `does VCAT think it may not be enforceable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT (a presidential member) considers it may not be practicable to enforce, or supervise compliance with, the agreement (answer no if unsure)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must VCAT register my agreement` MEANS
    `s 120 -- VCAT must register my agreement` `is the record signed by each party` `has the Commission certified it` `did I notify the other party in writing` `does VCAT think it may not be enforceable`

@export May I ask VCAT for an interim order to stop the other party prejudicing my dispute at the Commission (Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) s 121)? Only before an application under s 122 about the dispute has been made; an order lasts up to 28 days, and may be extended.
GIVEN `did I bring the dispute to the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you brought the dispute to the Commission
      `have I applied to VCAT under s 122` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an application to VCAT under s 122 about the dispute has already been made
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May I apply for an interim order` MEANS
    `s 121 -- I may apply for an interim order` `did I bring the dispute to the Commission` `have I applied to VCAT under s 122`

@export Can VCAT order the person to pay me compensation for my loss, damage or injury (Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) s 125)? Only once it finds a contravention; it may instead order them to stop, or to do something to redress the loss, or decline to act; if it finds none it dismisses the application.
GIVEN `did VCAT find a contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT has found that the person contravened Part 4, 6, 6A or 7
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can VCAT order compensation` MEANS
    `s 125 -- VCAT may order compensation` `did VCAT find a contravention`

@export Can the Commission enforce my VCAT order for me (Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) s 126)? Where VCAT made an order in your favour that has not been complied with, and you consent.
GIVEN `did VCAT make an order for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT found a contravention and made an order under s 125(a) (stop, compensate, redress)
      `has the person failed to comply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person has failed to comply with it
      `do I consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you consent to the Commission enforcing it
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the Commission enforce my order` MEANS
    `s 126 -- the Commission may enforce my order` `did VCAT make an order for me` `has the person failed to comply` `do I consent`
